==== Flash Layout ====
The GL-B1300 has one 32MiB SPI flash chip

^ Factory Layout for 32MiB SPI Flash //(spi0.0: MX25L25635E)// ^^^^^^^^^^^^
^ Layer0      | Raw NOR, Partitions from device tree |||||||||||
^ Layer1      | mtd0          | mtd1          | mtd2          | mtd3          | mtd4          | mtd5          | mtd6          | mtd7          | mtd8          | mtd9        ||
^ Layer2      |               |               |               |               |               |               |               |               |               |             | mtd10         |
^ Address     | ''0x00_0000'' | ''0x04_0000'' | ''0x06_0000'' | ''0x0c_0000'' | ''0x0d_0000'' | ''0x0e_0000'' | ''0x0f_0000'' | ''0x17_0000'' | ''0x18_0000'' | ''0x58_0000'' ||
^ Size        | 256 KiB       | 128 KiB       | 384 KiB       | 64 KiB        | 64 KiB        | 64 KiB        | 512 KiB       | 64 KiB        | 4 MiB         | 14.7 MiB | 12.4 MiB      |
^ Name **\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:SBL1 [Secondary Boot Loader]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:MIBIB [Multi-Image Boot Info Block]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:QSEE [Qualcomm Secure Execution Environment]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:CDT [Configuration Data Table]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:DDRPARAMS [DDR Parameters]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:APPSBLENV [Applications Processor Secondary Boot Loader Environment]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:APPSBL [Applications Processor Secondary Boot Loader]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:ART [Atheros Radio Test]</abbr>\\
  ** | **<abbr>0:HLOS [High-Level Operating System]</abbr>\\
  ** | **rootfs\\
  ** | **rootfs_data\\
  ** |
^ Usage //\\
  // | //Qualcomm\\ Bootloader ELF\\
  // | //Qualcomm\\ Partition Table\\
  // | //Qualcomm\\ TrustZone ELF\\
  // | //Qualcomm\\ Config\\
  // | //(empty, all 0xff)\\
  // | //U-Boot\\ Environment\\
  // | //U-Boot\\ ELF\\
  // | //Wi-Fi\\ Calibration\\
  // | //<abbr>FIT [Flattened Image Tree]</abbr> Kernel\\
  // | //[[docs:techref:filesystems#SquashFS]]\\ <color magenta>''/rom''</color>\\
  // | //[[docs:techref:filesystems#JFFS2]]\\ <color magenta>''/overlay''</color>\\
